  "title": "Week 45: I applied for e-Residency",
  "date": "2026-11-11T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 45: I applied for e-Residency\n\nRight now, my job-seeking VISA is half done. I have attended several interviews but have not received any offers.\nWith the AI trend, Estonia is going through a huge layoff wave. Every time I open my LinkedIn page, I see several posts about looking for new opportunities.\n\nCompared with jobs in Estonia and China, it is like two roads. The jobs I would like to apply for in Estonia are mostly at iGaming companies or global SaaS companies.\nThe Chinese ones, which I will start applying for next week, are more focused on Virtual Reality and FDE (Forward Deployed Engineering).\nOn both roads, I probably need Java skills, so I am rereading some Java knowledge, since I have not used Java for a long time.\n\nSince the job market is not very bright, I will consider investing in two possibilities. That said, I have started to apply for Estonia's e-Residency.\nThe application process is smooth. I write my motivation, upload a screenshot of my ID card and my photo, and then pay the 150 EUR fee. It will be 165 EUR next year.\nThe only caveat is that I have shaved for wearing masks because of the heavy cold I have right now.\n\nI hope the application passes. That will give me hope for the next 5 years. So what will the next 5 years hold?\n\nI may get a job in VR.\n\nI may start my own studio.\n\nI may go to Germany.\n\nI may not be doing anything related to coding...\n\nWho knows?",
